F8_fix: src/cli/forge.ts parses the --views list once. parseViewList(list) splits on the comma, trims each member, and drops the empty members, as the cut-out parser did on the base 23e551df. viewListSource(command, values) gives each command its list, and the preflight, the renderer (viewList), and the cut-out all read it. A trailing or doubled comma names the same views as the list without it: the cut-out wrote front.png for --views front, and exited 0.
C-P2-7_fix: the preflight uses the same normalization as the cut-out, so --views front, is accepted again and the cut-out writes its front PNG.
C-P2-1_fix: isNamedView(name) tests the named-view table with Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call, so constructor, toString, __proto__, and hasOwnProperty are unknown views. The renderer lookup uses the same own-property rule. Raw output: "Unknown view 'constructor'. Known: front, three-quarter, side, back, back-three-quarter, top, front-level, side-level". The refusal comes before the server starts, so no build runs and no output folder appears (GATE_D_PROBE_OUT_EXISTS=no).
F9_fix: checkOutputFolder(out) runs before the build and refuses a linked out/<name> or out/<name>/flat with one line. Raw output: "output folder is a link: out/<name>/flat" and "output folder is a link: out/<name>". The link is never followed: no flat PNG lands in the link target (GATE_D_LINK_TARGET_PNGS=0) and the other asset's flat folder keeps its marker (GATE_D_OTHER_FOLDER=marker.txt).
C-P2-8_fix: the linked destination is refused before the build, so the flat writer never writes through a link. removeFlatFolder keeps its realpath rule.
N2_note: the write no longer follows a planted link at all, because the linked destination is refused before the build.
